        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. UN force base in southern Lebanon comes under fire, one peacekeeper wounded Middle East Issued on: 14/03/2026 - 22:06 Modified: 14/03/2026 - 22:12 A UN peacekeeping base near the village of Mais al-Jabal in southern Lebanon came under fire, sparking a blaze that wounded one peacekeeper. UNIFIL is investigating the incident, said spokeswoman Kandice Ardiel, noting that \"the situation here in South Lebanon is precarious and volatile, not just for peacekeepers, but also for the civilians who live here and who have had to leave this area as well\". US embassy attacked in Baghdad, after strikes kill Iran-backed fighters in Iraq 14/03/2026 Middle East Israel and Lebanon are expected to hold direct talks in the coming days 14/03/2026 Middle East Israel threatens to strike ambulances in Lebanon in Hezbollah fighting 14/03/2026 Middle East Why did the US military bomb the strategic Iranian island of Kharg? 14/03/2026 Middle East Why did the US bomb Kharg Island? What is its significance for Iran? 14/03/2026 Middle East Israeli strike kills 12 medics in a clinic in southern Lebanon 14/03/2026 Middle East 14/03/2026 Middle East Lebanon says 26 paramedics were killed in Israeli strikes since March 2 14/03/2026 Middle East Iran threatens United Arab Emirate's ports and docks 14/03/2026 Middle East"
